I once saw (and tried to find again just now, but
couldn't) a line drawing of a eastern European
(Polish or Russian, I think) soldier in plate mail
and holding a round shield with a meter long spike
sticking out of the middle (and a sword in the other
hand).  Polish the shield, and shrink it a bit,
extend the spike to a lance, take off the arm straps
and put on a handle instead, and you have the makings
of a lance with a reflective polished shield as its
base.

How it would work for jousting I'm not sure, but I
seem to recall that real world jousting was done
with immense shields, so maybe OK.

